    leconEn: "Chowning found in 1973 that a vibrato pushed too far stops being a vibrato and becomes a timbre. The modulation index decides the number of sidebands: at one, two discreet lines either side; at thirty, a whole spectrum. One setting therefore travels the entire road from effect to timbre, which explains the process's commercial success.",
    condition: { sorte: "present", critere: { fiches: ["fm-synth"], parametre: { nom: "Modulation index", nomEn: "Modulation index", min: 30 }, rendu: true, quoi: "le synthétiseur FM", quoiEn: "the FM synth" } },
