    leconEn: "Below some fifty milliseconds a grain has no pitch of its own: the ear needs several periods to judge one, and two periods of a 440 hertz A last only five milliseconds. That is the boundary Gabor described in 1947 and which Xenakis, then Roads, took as material: below it you no longer compose notes but a density.",
    condition: { sorte: "present", critere: { fiches: ["granular-freeze"], parametre: { nom: "Taille", nomEn: "Grain size", max: 20 }, rendu: true, quoi: "le granular freeze", quoiEn: "the Granular Freeze" } },
