    leconEn: "A block chord and its arpeggio carry the same notes and do not say the same thing: the first gives a colour, the second a movement. The ear fuses simultaneous notes into one timbre — the very principle of additive synthesis — whereas spread over time they become a melody again. The same harmonic material changes nature with the rhythm it is given.",
